      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b93e4741e75674a7ea03e2f|full_name}: Not quite, EXTERNs are provided via \n\nUdonExternDelegate IUdonWrapperModule.GetExternFunctionDelegate(string signature)\n\nwhere UdonExternDelegate is (IUdonHeap heap, uint[] addresses) => void.\n\nIt's a function that takes the label and returns a corresponding delegate (if defined). Also, the format of label like \"SystemConvert.__ToString__SystemInt32__SystemString\" has nothing to do with the actual implementation of those wrappers.\n\nIt's also just a convention that the last address pushed to the stack is used to store a return value; wrappers can arbitrary read/write every address in the stack.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5dfd922a8ac300528b018ba0",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5dc8d6c9a956520f111d2229",
        "alias": "Remarkable Lynx",
