      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Summing up the discussion with Lyuma and JakEne on the Discord:\n\nThe label seems to follow the convention `<func-name>__<input-type1>_<input-type2>__<output-type>`, but we've found something weird. \n\nFor example, `GameObject.Find (static method)` and `Transform.Find (instance method)` have the same-ish name `Find__SystemString__UnityEngineTransform` and `Find__SystemString__UnityEngineGameObject`.\n\nJakEne says: \"it does appear that all object methods have an implicit this (probably SystemObject type)\".  This kind of inconsistency between static & instance method makes it hard to infer the actual type signature from the labels.\n\nWe, at least, need to create a strict and consistent convention for those EXTERN labels which is enough to extract the said informations, and make it documented, accessible via API (something like `string[] GetDefinedExternNames()`), and enforced.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
