      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Also, my proposed convention about EXTERNs which semantically have multiple outputs is to list all the `out` parameters at the end of the `__` separated list, so that `<func-name>__<input-type1>_<input-type2>__<output-type1>_<output-type2>`\n\nFor example, \n`SystemDateTime.__TryParse__SystemString_SystemIFormatProvider_SystemGlobalizationDateTimeStyles_SystemDateTimeRef__SystemBoolean`\nshould be instead named \n`SystemDateTime.__TryParse__SystemString_SystemIFormatProvider_SystemGlobalizationDateTimeStyles__SystemDateTime_SystemBoolean`.\nsince the 3rd and 4th address of the stack is used as output.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
