      "value": "Sorry for another long post. From the documentation and actual extern labels, I guess the current convention is:\n\n* For a static func from void to void, the label will be `__Foo__SystemVoid`. Let's call this *Type-S1*.\n* For a static func from void to T, it will be `__Foo__T`. *Type-S2*.\n* For a static func from T1,T2 to void, it will be `__Foo__T1_T2__SystemVoid`. *Type-S3*. \n* For a static func from T1,T2 to U, it will be `__Foo__T1_T2__U`. *Type-S4*.\n\nSimilarly, Type-I1 to Type-I4 is defined for instance functions.\n\nExamples:\nType-S1: `SystemTimeZoneInfo.__ClearCachedData__SystemVoid`\nType-S2: `SystemBoolean.__get_TrueString__SystemString`\nType-S3: `UnityEngineAnimatorUtility.__OptimizeTransformHierarchy__UnityEngineGameObject_SystemStringArray__SystemVoid`\nType-S4: `SystemBoolean.__op_Equality__SystemBoolean_SystemBoolean__SystemBoolean`\nType-I1: `SystemTimeZoneInfoArray.__Initialize__SystemVoid`\nType=I2: `SystemBoolean.__ToString__SystemString`\nType-I3: `SystemBooleanArray.__Set__SystemInt32_SystemBoolean__SystemVoid`\nType-I4: `SystemBoolean.__Equals__SystemObject__SystemBoolean`\n\nAlso, for label `L`, `GetExternFunctionParameterCount(L)` returns the number of stacks the extern func is expecting.\nLet's call it an *arity* of `L`.\n\nType-S1 funcs have arity 0. S2 have 1. S3 have n where n is the number of arguments. S4 have n+1.\n\nOn the other hand, instance funcs have an implicit argument corresponding to the instance. So I1 have 1, I2 have 2, I3 have n+1, and I4 have n+2.\nIt follows that we can distinguish between Type-Sk and Type-Ik funcs by looking at their arity.\n\n**There are 1069 (out of 21390) externs which contradict to the convention.**\n\nFor example, `UnityEngineAnimationsAimConstraint.__GetComponent__T` should have an arity 1 (if static) or 2 (if instance), but it has 3.\n\nAnother example is `VRCSDKBaseInputManager.__get__IsUsingHandController__SystemFuncSystemBoolean`.\nThis has an arity 1. I suspect that the `__` between `get` and `IsUsing..` is a duplicate, and it should just be `_` so that it now becomes Type-S2.\n\n---\n\nThe list of inconsistent functions is available here: https://gist.github.com/cannorin/0233147a6a5c3855c727ef9934f1108e\n\nAlso, here is the list of every function and its type (warning: it's very large): https://gist.github.com/cannorin/031aec897dd739791a115d18c82b1d90",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
