      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2019-12-22T08:36:45.533Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 1,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "5dfe518a081b520d52f8ee25",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5dfd806310ebbc6bff50f31c",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The 0th argument is an instance of `Component`. The 1st argument is the `Type` object of the 2nd argument, which will store the return value of `GetComponent<T>`.\n\nI'll add this to the parsing rule and retry.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5e0051c07c3d41477bab5f2e",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5dc8d6c9a956520f111d2229",
        "alias": "Remarkable Lynx",
        "aliasID": "65c80fbded6eefce4cecb134",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/1fe82504e59b322ed250ccba87ce1479.png",
        "created": "2019-11-11T03:34:33.029Z",
        "name": "cannorin",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5df404cc2072644ac4b5e385",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2019-12-23T05:33:52.646Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 0,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5dfd806310ebbc6bff50f31c",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Ok, I updated the logic to recognize generic functions, and still found 61 inconsistently-named functions: \nhttps://gist.github.com/cannorin/0233147a6a5c3855c727ef9934f1108e\n\nBut the logic around generic functions is very ad-hoc. We need a better syntax to represent those functions, like `UnityEngineAnimationsAimConstraint.__GetComponent<T>__T`.\n\nWithout such syntax, we cannot distinguish, say,  a static function with one generic type parameter (which has an arity n+1+1 because it accepts one additional implicit `Type` object) from a member function with no generic type parameter (which also has an arity n+1+1).\n\nAlso here is the updated list of all externs: https://gist.github.com/cannorin/031aec897dd739791a115d18c82b1d90",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5e0052c6e4b27a2bc1c26914",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5dc8d6c9a956520f111d2229",
        "alias": "Remarkable Lynx",
        "aliasID": "65c80fbded6eefce4cecb134",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/1fe82504e59b322ed250ccba87ce1479.png",
        "created": "2019-11-11T03:34:33.029Z",
        "name": "cannorin",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5df404cc2072644ac4b5e385",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2019-12-23T05:38:14.512Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 2,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5dfd806310ebbc6bff50f31c",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 6
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Also I want to emphasize that **it is very, very unreasonable to extract type informations only from label names and arities, which can only be obtained from reflection (because they are in private fields)**.\n\nThe fact we can workaround it (as shown below) is **not** a reason not to implement decent metadata APIs.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5e327858f907b86822320e94",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5bf03df114e6332c1a0dc44d",
        "alias": "Flax Swordtail",
        "aliasID": "660d0f57e5d26962aa5e5749",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/6d5e622d8e50c2e62a901160b8adc8ee.png",
        "created": "2018-11-17T16:12:33.834Z",
        "name": "Ilya",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5df404cc2072644ac4b5e385",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2020-01-30T06:31:52.856Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 0,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5dfd806310ebbc6bff50f31c",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Eventhough there is access to type information (GetRegistries() method, which is used to generate available graph nodes in editor) it feels more like hack than official-way api for 3-rd party udon assembly generation tools (like compilers).\nAlso i want to mention that this information is even not enough.\nI personally would like to have some sort of info about what type can be casted to what. Of course i can just find this information based on corresponding .net types (reflection) but there is no guarantee that if .net type (for example int) could be casted to other type (for example long) - it's also true in udon vm's world.\nI need that information for implicit typecasting abilities at least (for finding best method overload without need to explicitly cast every parameter to very specific type).\nSo it would be nice if developers would add some separate library with all that data for given sdk version, or say, some web service for fetching that data for specified sdk version, or whatever they decide is better. I mean, graph mechanics is likely to stay the same, but available api's is to be changing over and over from version to version (of sdk). So just documentation would be very painful to support all that (it's alot of types and methods out there).\nI'm making Doshik lang compiler",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5e3d58fd42022c69fb2d510a",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5dc8d6c9a956520f111d2229",
        "alias": "Remarkable Lynx",
        "aliasID": "65c80fbded6eefce4cecb134",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/1fe82504e59b322ed250ccba87ce1479.png",
        "created": "2019-11-11T03:34:33.029Z",
        "name": "cannorin",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5df404cc2072644ac4b5e385",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2020-02-07T12:33:01.862Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
