      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5dfd806310ebbc6bff50f31c",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've just started to provide the metadata in JSON format: https://github.com/cannorin/UdonInfoExtractor\n`udon_externs.json` contains the metadata of extern functions, `udon_types.json` contains the type infomation (including subtyping relations!), and `udon_info.json` contains both.\nHope this helps.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-12-21T02:16:03.075Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm trying to write a compiler for UdonVM, but the dynamic nature of EXTERN functions prevents us from writing a static analyzer (e.g. type checking).\nWe need at least:\n- Names of EXTERNS\n- API to get the following info per EXTERN:\n    - expected types for each stack element in array\n   - the usage per element, argument (\"in\" in C#) or overwritable argument (\"ref\" in C#) or return value (\"out\" in C#).\nDocumentation is not enough. We need a programmatical access for those information.",
